jank-34: the call site calls a variadic fn's variadic arity directly, and computes a multimethod's
dispatch and method lookup inline (cohost doc/upstream/jank-34-callsite-variadic-multi.md; lane U7,
order U7-4)

Base: jank-lang/jank f3d82d65499920f81216e9235bd5d3a34a968e3f with the series before it in
upstream/jank/patches/series (... 27, 28, 30, 29, 32). Apply from the clone's root: git apply <this file>.

Builds on 24-direct-calls (call_fast) and 29-variadic-multi (stack rest args, the multimethod cache
fix, keyword dispatch inline).

Files:
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/analyze/processor.cpp, include .../analyze/expr/call.hpp:
  - a registry of each var's variadic shape as of its last analyzed def (the variadic arity's
    required count, the fixed arities). A call whose head is such a var, with at least the
    required args and no fixed arity of its count, is marked variadic_direct.
  - a call whose head var holds a multimethod when the call is analyzed is marked multi_direct.
  - both only at -Odirect-call (the -O3 default); -Ono-direct-call turns both off.
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/ir/{processor,builder}.cpp, include .../ir/{builder,instruction}.hpp:
  the marks ride on inst::dynamic_call.
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/codegen/cpp_processor.cpp: emits
  jank::runtime::call_variadic_direct<P>(f, args...) or jank::runtime::call_multi_direct(f, args...)
  in place of call_fast.
- compiler+runtime/include/cpp/jank/runtime/core/call_direct.hpp (new; included from prelude.hpp):
  - call_variadic_direct<P>: when the fn object read at the call is a jit_variadic_function (a
    realized deferred fn's compiled one) whose variadic arity still takes P required params (and,
    for exactly P args, has no fixed arity of P), it calls arity_{P+1} directly with the fixed args
    and the rest sequence: on the caller's stack when 29's rest_noescape bit is set, else one packed
    allocation. No arity switch, no virtual call. Anything else (a redefinition, with-redefs, a
    binding, a closure) takes call_fast.
  - call_multi_direct: when the object is a multi_function, the dispatch value of a one-argument
    call is computed inline (a get of the dispatch key, or the dispatch constant), else the dispatch
    fn is called through call_fast. The method is read from the cache entries under the hierarchy
    compare (identical dispatch value), else from get_fn, and called through call_fast.
- compiler+runtime/include/cpp/jank/runtime/obj/multi_function.hpp, src/.../multi_function.cpp:
  - dispatch_kind / dispatch_key: a keyword dispatch fn is kind key (as 29 computed it); a new
    constructor takes a shape from defmulti.
  - the one-entry method cache is two entries, so two alternating dispatch values both hit. A miss
    fills only an empty or stale entry (no allocation per call, three or more values stay on the
    map).
- compiler+runtime/src/jank/clojure/core.jank (defmulti), include .../runtime/core.hpp,
  src/.../runtime/core.cpp (a multi_fn overload): defmulti reads the dispatch form. A one-param fn
  returning a literal ((fn [x] 0)) is :constant; one getting a keyword from its param ((fn [x] (:k x)),
  (fn [x] (get x :k))) is :key. Anything else is unchanged.

Measured (lane U7-4; box shared, no lock, load 3.8-4.6; 3 interleaved rounds vs the series without
34, built on the series through 32 without 31; the whole series applies clean with 31):
- run.sh 34-callsite, medians ns per 1e7, series / +34: call-variadic 84071982 / 66802207 (2.10x
  call-2, bar 3x); multi-one-method 108766633 / 53802477 (1.68x fn-call, bar 2x);
  multi-two-methods-alternating 215406823 / 96621896 (3.02x fn-call, bar 2x not met: an arbitrary
  dispatch fn is still called); multi-keyword-alternating 222806755 / 118583975. Every correctness
  line Clojure's values on both.
- -Ono-direct-call: call-variadic 360843495 (the stack and direct paths off); values unchanged.
- run.sh 29, 24, 22, 20: value lines unchanged. bb boot:jank 542/171/78/0, battery 147/149 (as the
  series), libraries 61/61.

